<title>UK: BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE COLLATED RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE COLLATED RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of first leg</p>
<p>matches in the men's EuroLeague basketball elimination round</p>
<p>played on Thursday:</p>
<p>In Belgrade:</p>
<p>Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 71 Olympiakos (Greece) 81</p>
<p>(halftime 36-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Partizan -  Haris Brkic 13, Miroslav Beric 12</p>
<p>Olympiakos - Franko Nakic 27, David Rivers 14</p>
<p>In Istanbul:</p>
<p>Efes Pilsen (Turkey) 76 Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel) 67 (43-36)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Efes Pilsen - Sarica 20, Karasev 15</p>
<p>Maccabi Elite - Johnson 18, White 15</p>
<p>In Berlin:</p>
<p>Alba Berlin (Germnay) 77 FC Barcelona (Spain) 95 (41-53)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Alba Berlin - Wendell Alexis 25, Henning Harnisch 13</p>
<p>FC Barcelona - Andres Jimenez 19, Javier Fernandez 15,</p>
<p>Roberto Duenas 13</p>
<p>In Milan:</p>
<p>Stefanel Milan (Italy) 67 Kinder Bologna (Italy) 59  (37-28)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Stefanel - Gregor Fucka 23, Anthony Bowie 10, Flavio</p>
<p>Portaluppi 10, Alessandro De Pol 10</p>
<p>Kinder - Kostas Patavoukas 16, Zoran Savic 12, Alessandro</p>
<p>Abbio 11</p>
<p>Attendance - 5,000</p>
<p>In Zagreb:</p>
<p>Cibona Zagreb (Croatia) 61  Smelt Olimpija (Slovenia) 58</p>
<p>(29-29)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Cibona: Damir Mulaomerovic 21, Djevad Alihodzic 12, Evgeny</p>
<p>Kissourine 10.</p>
<p>Olimpija: Henrie 14, Milic 13, Kraljevic 8.</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000.</p>
<p>In Athens:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos (Greece) 68  Limoges (France) 67 (37-30)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos - Economou 21, Nicola 10, Dinkins 10</p>
<p>Limoge - Bonato 18, Ruffin 18, Markovic 11</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>Second leg matches to be played on Tuesday, March 11.</p>
</text>
